            <ArticleTitle>Lacrimal gland myxoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>887-889</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/ijo.IJO_226_17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myxomas are rare neoplasms of mesenchymal origin. Cases of conjunctival, corneal, and orbital myxomas have been reported in the literature; however, to the best of our knowledge, there is no report of a lacrimal gland myxoma. We report a case of an orbital myxoma involving the lacrimal gland and its management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
